Description:

reconstruct now repairs JMAP mailbox id clashes, and its -I uniqueid repair
works for mailboxes that keep their files under the uniqueid.  A mailbox
record written with the id of another live mailbox is logged as
event=mboxlist.mailboxid.clash.


Documentation:

docsrc/reference/manpages/systemcommands/reconstruct.rst
docsrc/developer/logfmt.md


Config changes:

None.


Upgrade instructions:

Sites that have seen two folders of one user report the same JMAP mailbox id
should run "reconstruct -u <user>" on the master; the new id replicates.
The repaired mailbox appears as created in Mailbox/changes.

Shared mailboxes under a virtual domain now have their id lookup key scoped
to the domain, matching the counters their ids come from.  The first
reconstruct of such a mailbox rewrites its record to add the key.


